---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/global/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import HeroText from '../../components/hero/HeroText.astro';
import CtaBand from '../../components/sections/CtaBand.astro';
---

<Base
  title="New Build Roofing Contractor Leeds | WW Roofing"
  description="New-build roofing in Leeds and Yorkshire: membrane, battens, coverings and leadwork to specification and programme, for self-builders and site developers."
>
  <HeroText
    kicker="Construction / Leeds"
    heading="New-build roofing"
    lede="From single self-build plots to development sites, we deliver the roofing package: set out and covered to specification, weathered in properly, and finished when the programme says it will be."
  />

  <div class="wrap" style="padding-block-start: var(--space-4)">
    <Breadcrumbs
      items={[
        { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
        { label: 'Construction', href: '/construction/' },
        { label: 'New builds' },
      ]}
    />
  </div>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>For self-builders</h2>
      <p>
        If you are building your own house, the roof is the milestone that makes
        everything else possible: once it is watertight, the trades inside can start. We
        work from your architect's drawings, advise on coverings and details where the
        specification leaves room, and get you weathertight without drama.
      </p>
      <h2>For sites and developers</h2>
      <p>
        On multi-plot sites we price per plot or per package, keep to the build
        sequence, and coordinate with your site management on access, lifting and
        inspections. If you are a main contractor looking for a roofing subcontractor,
        the <a href="/sectors/construction-partners/">construction partners page</a>
        covers how we work in more detail.
      </p>
      <h2>Straight answers</h2>
      <p>
        New-build roofing is specification-led, so we quote against the drawings and
        say clearly what is included and what is provisional. If a detail on the
        drawings will not work on the roof, we say so before it is built, not after.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    title="Pricing a new build?"
    note="Send the roof drawings and specification and we will come back with a clear package price."
  />
</Base>
